IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gp-dates`
IMPORT `gp-part4a`
IMPORT `gp-seat`
IMPORT `gp-seat-plaintiff`

-- Supreme Court Act 1986 (Vic), Part 4A -- worked cases for the representative plaintiff's questions (gp-seat-plaintiff.l4),
-- with mirror cases: the same facts asked from the group member's seat (gp-seat.l4), with answers that agree. Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim
-- about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 33C, 33D -- bringing the group proceeding`

-- Arguments: persons with claims, same circumstances, common question, kind, cross-vesting only, I have a claim, sufficient
-- interest.
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 7 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 7 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 7 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 6 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 6 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 40 TRUE TRUE `a proceeding concerning property subject to a trust` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 40 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 33D(2).
#ASSERT `May I continue after my own claim ends` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I continue after my own claim ends` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 33ZD, 33ZDA, 33ZJ -- costs`

#ASSERT `Who answers for the defendant's costs, as plaintiff` TRUE EQUALS `the law practice representing the plaintiff and group members, which must also give any security for costs ordered (s 33ZDA(2))`
#ASSERT `Who answers for the defendant's costs, as plaintiff` FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff, if the Court so orders (s 33ZD(1)(a))`

#ASSERT `May the Court make a group costs order on my application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Court make a group costs order on my application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the Court make a group costs order on my application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 30% of $3,000,000 is $900,000.
#ASSERT `What are the legal costs under the order, as plaintiff` TRUE 30 3000000 EQUALS JUST 900000
#ASSERT `What are the legal costs under the order, as plaintiff` FALSE 30 3000000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- $820,000 incurred, $600,000 recoverable: at most $220,000; $1 over: $1.
#ASSERT `How much of my costs can come out of the damages` TRUE TRUE 820000 600000 EQUALS 220000
#ASSERT `How much of my costs can come out of the damages` TRUE TRUE 600001 600000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How much of my costs can come out of the damages` TRUE TRUE 600000 600000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my costs can come out of the damages` FALSE TRUE 820000 600000 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 33V, 33W -- settling`

#ASSERT `May I settle or discontinue the group proceeding` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I settle or discontinue the group proceeding` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I settle my own claim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I settle my own claim` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: settled, notice given, notice in time, substitute ordered.
#ASSERT `Can I stop being the plaintiff` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I stop being the plaintiff` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I stop being the plaintiff` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I stop being the plaintiff` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I stop being the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 33P -- leaving Part 4A`

#ASSERT `May I continue on my own claim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I continue on my own claim` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Mirror cases: the same facts from both seats`

-- Twelve investors, same circumstances, a common question: the member may have the claim brought, and the plaintiff (with a
-- claim and a sufficient interest) may bring it.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought as a group proceeding` 12 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE EQUALS `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 12 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought as a group proceeding` 6 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE EQUALS `Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` 6 TRUE TRUE `a claim of any other kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Who answers for the defendant's costs, with and without a group costs order.
#ASSERT `Who pays the defendant's costs` TRUE EQUALS `Who answers for the defendant's costs, as plaintiff` TRUE
#ASSERT `Who pays the defendant's costs` FALSE EQUALS `Who answers for the defendant's costs, as plaintiff` FALSE
-- The legal costs under a 30% order on $3,000,000.
#ASSERT `What are the legal costs under the group costs order` TRUE 30 3000000 EQUALS `What are the legal costs under the order, as plaintiff` TRUE 30 3000000
-- The s 33ZJ payment out of the damages, seen by the member and by the plaintiff.
#ASSERT `How much of the damages may go to the plaintiff's costs` TRUE TRUE 820000 600000 EQUALS `How much of my costs can come out of the damages` TRUE TRUE 820000 600000
-- Settlement needs approval, from either seat.
#ASSERT `May the group proceeding be settled` FALSE EQUALS `May I settle or discontinue the group proceeding` FALSE
